class_name ThresholdEnemyData
extends RefCounted
## Level 4 — The Threshold — enemy definitions.
##
## Two packs, split by depth, because the biome's identity is "someone opened a door they
## could not hold": the shallows are the cult still holding it, the deeps are what came
## through. Minifantasy_Dark_Brotherhood supplies phases 1-3, Minifantasy_Dark_Orc_Army
## supplies phases 4-5, and the Possessed tier is the hinge between them — the cult after
## the thing it summoned got inside it.
##
## Seventeen rank-and-file roles; the miniboss and final boss live in their own factories
## (RitualGuardData / PaleChampionData) because bosses carry choreographed skills.
##
##   ── the cult (Cannon_Fodder) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
##   th_fodder       Acolyte             — fragile melee swarm
##   th_swarmer      Cult Hound          — fastest unit, paper-thin
##   th_zealot       Zealot              — standard melee
##   ── the devoted (Devoted_Brothers) ───────────────────────────────────────
##   th_skirmisher   Devoted Blade       — armoured melee
##   th_sentinel     Devoted Sentinel    — slower, meatier melee
##   th_archer       Devoted Stalker     — ranged, the only real projectile sheet in either pack
##   ── the chosen (Choosen_Ones) ────────────────────────────────────────────
##   th_caster       Dark Channeler      — ranged, void bolt
##   th_flagellant   Flagellant          — high damage, low armour; hurts itself to hurt you
##   ── the possessed (Possessed) ────────────────────────────────────────────
##   th_possessed    Dark Cultist        — the Zealot's role, after
##   th_hound        Dark Hound          — fast AND heavy, which nothing else is
##   th_abomination  Dark Abomination    — brute
##   ── the army (Dark_Orc_Army) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
##   th_raider       Orc Raider          — army melee
##   th_berserker    Warbreed Berserker  — aggressive, fast for its weight
##   th_phalanx      Warbreed Phalanx    — armour wall; the biome's armour check
##   th_arbalist     Warbreed Arbalist   — elite ranged
##   th_warg         Warg                — the army's fast beast
##   th_troll        Cave Troll          — heaviest rank-and-file
##
## Scenes are generated by tools/gen_threshold_scenes.gd. Registered in EnemyRegistry.
##
## Scaling intent: biome 4 sits roughly 1.3x the equivalent Nightmare Realm role. NMRealm
## reference: fodder 20hp/10dmg, swarmer 14/9 spd150, skirmisher 33/14/3armor,
## raider 55/19/5, brute 95/26/7, heavy 150/34/10.
##
## DELIBERATELY UNWIRED SHEETS, and why — the full-utilization rule wants a reason, not
## silence:
##   - Dark_Channeler/Possess_Acolyte, Possess_Hound, Possess_Zealot. These are 2-row
##     sequences of a *named lesser unit* being taken over, i.e. a mid-life transform from
##     one enemy into another. enemy.gd has no transform hook — the same limitation that
##     left the Monster pack's Werewolf/Transformation unwired, where the two shapes
##     shipped as two separate units instead. The Channeler still casts with Possess.png,
##     so the gesture is on screen; only the target-swap is missing.
##   - The whole Feral_Orcs tier, plus Lesser Orc_Blade / Orc_Scout and Warbreed_Blade.
##     The orc pack is three rank tiers of the same four archetypes, so wiring every tier
##     makes late waves read as recolours of early ones. One tier of each silhouette ships;
##     Orc_Raider survives from Lesser because its Bite sheet makes it a different animal.

